  "body": "What happens: on `main` (e8a7f59), `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test probe_op -- every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag` fails:\n\n```\nassert_eq!(project::PROJECT_VERSION, 51, \"the probe arrives without a format rung\");\nleft: 52, right: 51\n```\n\nThe v52 rung (#329, \"a work-offset height stops naming its own slot\") bumped `PROJECT_VERSION` without touching this line; #196 had already moved it once (50 -> 51). Every future rung (#326 / PR #341 brings v53) breaks it again.\n\nExpected: the test pins what it says - that adding the Probe kind kept every older kind's stored id and digest tag, so the probe needed no format rung. The kind-order loop above the assert already proves that; the hard-coded version number proves nothing about the probe and goes stale on every unrelated rung.\n\nFound while gating #340 (the failure is the same on unchanged main).\n\nDone means: the test no longer pins the current project version; it keeps the id/tag asserts.\n",
